1: # GradePulse
2: 
3: A self-learning personalization engine for education, powered by Contextual Bandit algorithms.
4: 
5: ## Why This Matters
6: 
7: In Nigeria and across Africa, teachers manage 40-80 students per class with no way to personalize learning. A student struggling with fractions gets the same content as one ready for algebra. GradePulse changes that — it learns what works for each student and recommends the right content at the right time, using the teacher's existing weekly test scores as its signal.
8: 
9: Most LMS platforms are content repositories. GradePulse is a recommendation engine that gets smarter with every score a teacher enters.
10: 
11: ## What It Does
12: 
13: Every student is different. Most LMS platforms serve the same content to everyone. The Brain learns **what works for whom** — adapting in real-time as each student interacts with the platform.
14: 
15: ```
16: ┌─────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐
17: │ Student      │────>│ Brain recommends │────>│ Student      │
18: │ (context)    │     │ (explore/exploit)│     │ engages with │
19: └─────────────┘     └──────────────────┘     │ content      │
20:                                              └──────┬───────┘
21:                                                     │
22: ┌─────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐            │
23: │ Brain       │<────│ Reward signal    │<───────────┘
24: │ updates     │     │ (score, complete)│
25: │ matrices    │     └──────────────────┘
26: └─────────────┘
27: ```
28: 
29: ## Key Features
30: 
31: | Capability | What It Means |
32: |---|---|
33: | **2 Algorithms** | Disjoint LinUCB and Hybrid LinUCB with online clustering |
34: | **Real-time Learning** | Updates after every interaction — no batch retraining |
35: | **Cold-start Ready** | Explores when it has no data; exploits when it does |
36: | **Self-Diagnostics** | Neural Score measures 7 dimensions of model health |
37: | **Online Clustering** | Groups similar students to share knowledge (COBART-style) |
38: | **FastAPI REST API** | Production-ready REST API with demo seeding |
39: | **Multi-Tenant** | School-scoped data model with class management |
40: | **Multi-Worker Safe** | File-based brain state sync with locking — safe for multiple uvicorn workers |
41: | **Data Ingestion** | CLI tool for pilot-school data (CSV/Excel) with 17-dim context vector validation |
42: 
43: ## Neural Score — Built-in Diagnostics
44: 
45: The Brain scores itself on 7 dimensions (each 0–10):
46: 
47: ```
48: Exploration Efficiency  →  8.3/10  (Are we trying diverse content?)
49: Reward Convergence      →  7.1/10  (Is average reward improving?)
50: Context Sensitivity     →  6.8/10  (Do different students get different recs?)
51: Recommendation Precision→  7.5/10  (Are recommended items getting good rewards?)
52: Grade Prediction        →  6.2/10  (Can we forecast student performance?)
53: Cohort Purity           →  7.0/10  (Are student clusters well-separated?)
54: Objective Balance       →  7.5/10  (Are all reward signals being used?)
55: ─────────────────────────────────
56: NEURAL SCORE            →  7.2/10
57: ```
